The King James Version, as published in 1611, is in the public domain.
The original text — including the 1611 spelling and typography reproduced in
bible/kjv1611/ — is therefore free of copyright.

This repository is a repackaging of that public-domain text into JSON, and is
likewise placed in the public domain.

You may copy, modify, distribute and use these files, including commercially,
without permission or attribution.

The text is offered without warranty of any kind. Some editions differ in
chapter divisions, verse numbering, spelling and the handling of the
Apocrypha, so verify against a critical edition before relying on it for
scholarly work.